{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-1","title":"Mark 3:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Christ heals the withered hand, 10 and many other infirmities; 11 rebukes the unclean spirit; 13 chooses his twelve apostles; 22 convinces the blasphemy of casting out devils by Beelzebub; 31 and shows who are his brother, sister, and mother.</p>\n<p>he entered. 1:21; Mt 12:9-14; Lu 6:6-11 withered. 1Ki 13:4; Joh 5:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-2","title":"Mark 3:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Ps 37:32; Isa 29:20,21; Jer 20:10; Da 6:4; Lu 6:7; 11:53,54; 14:1 Lu 20:20; Joh 9:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-3","title":"Mark 3:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>he saith. Isa 42:4; Da 6:10; Lu 6:8; Joh 9:4; 1Co 15:58; Ga 6:9 Php 1:14,28-30; 1Pe 4:1 Stand forth. or, Arise, stand forth in the midst.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-4","title":"Mark 3:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Is it. 2:27,28; Ho 6:6; Mt 12:10-12; Lu 6:9; 13:13-17; 14:1-5 But. 9:34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-5","title":"Mark 3:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>with anger.With anger at their desperate malice and wickedness, and with commiseration for the calamities which they would thereby bring on themselves.</p>\n<p>Lu 6:10; 13:15; Eph 4:26; Re 6:16 grieved. Ge 6:6; Jud 10:16; Ne 13:8; Ps 95:10; Isa 63:9,10; Lu 19:40-44 Eph 4:30; Heb 3:10,17 hardness. or, blindness. Isa 6:9,10; 42:18-20; 44:18-20; Mt 13:14,15; Ro 11:7-10,25 2Co 3:14; Eph 4:18 Stretch. 1Ki 13:6; Mt 12:13; Lu 6:10; 17:14; Joh 5:8,9; 9:7; Heb 5:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-6","title":"Mark 3:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Pharisees. Ps 109:3,4; Mt 12:14; Lu 6:11; 20:19,20; 22:2; Joh 11:53 Herodians. 8:15; 12:13; Mt 22:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-7","title":"Mark 3:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Jesus. Mt 10:23; 12:15; Lu 6:12; Joh 10:39-41; 11:53,54; Ac 14:5,6 Ac 17:10,14 and a. Mt 4:25; Lu 6:17 Galilee. 1:39; Jos 20:7; 21:32; Lu 23:5; Joh 7:41,52</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-8","title":"Mark 3:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Idumea. Isa 34:5; Eze 35:15; 36:5; Mal 1:2-4 Edom. beyond. Nu 32:33-38; Jos 13:8-14 Tyre. 7:24,31; Jos 19:28,29; Ps 45:12; 87:4; Isa 23:1-18; Eze 26:1-28:26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-9","title":"Mark 3:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>because. 5:30; Joh 6:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-10","title":"Mark 3:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>he had. Mt 12:15; 14:14 pressed. or, rushed. touched. 5:27,28; 6:56; Mt 14:36; Ac 5:15; 19:11,12 and many. 5:29; Ge 12:17; Nu 11:33; Lu 7:2; Heb 12:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-11","title":"Mark 3:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>unclean. 1:23,24; 5:5,6; Mt 8:31; Lu 4:41; Ac 16:17; 19:13-17; Jas 2:19 the Son. 1:1; Mt 4:3,6; 8:29; 14:33; Lu 8:28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-12","title":"Mark 3:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>1:25,34; Mt 12:16; Ac 16:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-13","title":"Mark 3:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Mt 10:1-4; Lu 6:12-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-14","title":"Mark 3:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>he ordained. Joh 15:16; Ac 1:24,25; Ga 1:1,15-20 and. Lu 9:1-6; 10:1-11; 24:47; Ac 1:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-16","title":"Mark 3:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>Simon. 1:16; Mt 16:16-18; Joh 1:42; 1Co 1:12; 3:22; 9:5; Ga 2:7-9 Cephas. 2Pe 1:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-17","title":"Mark 3:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>James. 1:19,20; 5:37; 9:2; 10:35; 14:33; Joh 21:2,20-25; Ac 12:1 he surnamed. Isa 58:1; Jer 23:29; Heb 4:12; Re 10:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-18","title":"Mark 3:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>Andrew. Joh 1:40; 6:8; 12:21,22; Ac 1:13 Philip. Joh 1:43-45; 6:5-7; 14:8,9 Bartholomew. Mt 10:3; Lu 6:14; Ac 1:13 Matthew. 2:14; Mt 9:9; Lu 5:27-29 Levi. Lu 6:15 Thomas. Joh 11:16; 20:24-29; 21:2; Ac 1:13 James. 6:3; Mt 10:3; 13:55; Lu 6:15; Ac 15:13; 21:18; 1Co 9:5; 15:7; Ga 1:19 Ga 2:9; Jas 1:1 Alphaeus. 2:14 Thaddaeus. Mt 10:3; Lu 6:16; Joh 14:22; Ac 1:13 Judas the brother of James. Jude 1:1 Simon. Mt 10:4; Lu 6:15; Ac 1:13 Simon Zelotes. Canaanite.[Kananites ,] so called, not from being a native of Canaan, [Chanaan ,] which would have been [Chananaos,] but from the Hebrew Kana, to be zealous, whence he is called in Greek [Zelotes ,] Zelotes, or the Zealot, from [Zeloo ,] to be zealous.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-19","title":"Mark 3:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>Judas. Mt 26:14-16,47; 27:3-5; Joh 6:64,71; 12:4-6; 13:2,26-30 Ac 1:16-25 into an house. or, home.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-20","title":"Mark 3:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>so that. 9; 6:31; Lu 6:17; Joh 4:31-34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-21","title":"Mark 3:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>when.Some render, \"And they who were with him (in the house, ver. 19,) hearing (the noise) went out to restrain, ([auton, i.e., ochlos ,] the multitude,) for they said, It (the mob) is mad.\" This, however, is contrary to all the versions; and appears an unnatural construction.</p>\n<p>friends. or, kinsmen. 31; Joh 7:3-10 He is. 2Ki 9:11; Jer 29:26; Ho 9:7; Joh 10:20; Ac 26:24; 2Co 5:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-22","title":"Mark 3:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>which. 7:1; Mt 15:1; Lu 5:17 He hath. Ps 22:6; Mt 9:34; 10:25; 12:24; Lu 11:15; Joh 7:20; 8:48,52; 10:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-23","title":"Mark 3:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>in parables. Ps 49:4; Mt 13:34 How. Mt 12:25-30; Lu 11:17-23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-24","title":"Mark 3:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>Jud 9:23-57; 12:1-6; 2Sa 20:1,6; 1Ki 12:16-20; Isa 9:20,21; 19:2,3 Eze 37:22; Zec 11:14; Joh 17:21; 1Co 1:10-13; Eph 4:3-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-25","title":"Mark 3:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>Ge 13:7,8; 37:4; Ps 133:1; Ga 5:15; Jas 3:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-27","title":"Mark 3:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>Ge 3:15; Isa 27:1; 49:24-26; 53:12; 61:1; Mt 12:29; Lu 10:17-20 Lu 11:21-23; Joh 12:31; Ro 16:20; Eph 6:10-13; Col 2:15; Heb 2:14 1Jo 3:8; 4:4; Re 12:7-9; 20:1-3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-28","title":"Mark 3:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>Mt 12:31,32; Lu 12:10; Heb 6:4-8; 10:26-31; 1Jo 5:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-29","title":"Mark 3:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>but is. 12:40; Mt 25:46; 2Th 1:9; Jude 1:7,13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-30","title":"Mark 3:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>22; Joh 10:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-31","title":"Mark 3:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>Mt 12:46-48; Lu 8:19-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-33","title":"Mark 3:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>Who. De 33:9; Lu 2:49; Joh 2:4; 2Co 5:16 or. 21; 6:3; Joh 7:3-5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-34","title":"Mark 3:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>Behold. Ps 22:22; So 4:9,10; 5:1,2; Mt 12:49,50; 25:40-45; 28:10 Lu 11:27,28; Joh 20:17; Ro 8:29; Heb 2:11,12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-3-35","title":"Mark 3:35","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>do. Mt 7:21; Joh 7:17; Jas 1:25; 1Jo 2:17; 3:22,23</p>"}]}